{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"TITLE:\"AAV-mediated expression of proneural factors stimulates neurogenesis from adult Muller glia in vivo.\"","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":50,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"40050705","source":"MED","pmid":"40050705","pmcid":"PMC11982270","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC11982270"]},"doi":"10.1038/s44321-025-00209-3","title":"AAV-mediated expression of proneural factors stimulates neurogenesis from adult Müller glia in vivo.","authorString":"Pavlou M, Probst M, Kaplan L, Filippova E, Prieve AR, Rieke F, Reh TA.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Pavlou M","lastName":"Pavlou","firstName":"Marina","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8290-0656"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurobiology and Biophysics, University of Washington, Seattle, WA, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Probst M","lastName":"Probst","firstName":"Marlene","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0006-4476-6851"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurobiology and Biophysics, University of Washington, Seattle, WA, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Kaplan L","lastName":"Kaplan","firstName":"Lew","initials":"L","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurobiology and Biophysics, University of Washington, Seattle, WA, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Filippova E","lastName":"Filippova","firstName":"Elizaveta","initials":"E","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Agricultural and Biological Engineering, Purdue University, Lafayette, IN, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Prieve AR","lastName":"Prieve","firstName":"Aric R","initials":"AR","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurobiology and Biophysics, University of Washington, Seattle, WA, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Rieke F","lastName":"Rieke","firstName":"Fred","initials":"F","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurobiology and Biophysics, University of Washington, Seattle, WA, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Reh TA","lastName":"Reh","firstName":"Thomas A","initials":"TA","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3524-0886"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurobiology and Biophysics, University of Washington, Seattle, WA, USA. CONTACT_EMAIL."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3524-0886"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8290-0656"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0006-4476-6851"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data","related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"4","volume":"17","journalIssueId":3928189,"dateOfPublication":"2025 Apr","monthOfPublication":4,"yearOfPublication":2025,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"EMBO Mol Med","title":"EMBO molecular medicine","essn":"1757-4684","issn":"1757-4676","nlmid":"101487380","isoabbreviation":"EMBO Mol Med"},"printPublicationDate":"2025-04-01"},"pubYear":"2025","pageInfo":"722-746","abstractText":"The lack of regeneration in the human central nervous system (CNS) has major health implications. To address this, we previously used transgenic mouse models to show that neurogenesis can be stimulated in the adult mammalian retina by driving regeneration programs that other species activate following injury. Expression of specific proneural factors in adult Müller glia causes them to re-enter the cell cycle and give rise to new neurons following retinal injury. To bring this strategy closer to clinical application, we now show that neurogenesis can also be stimulated when delivering these transcription factors to Müller glia using adeno-associated viral (AAV) vectors. AAV-mediated neurogenesis phenocopies the neurogenesis we observed from transgenic animals, with different proneural factor combinations giving rise to distinct neuronal subtypes in vivo. Vector-borne neurons are morphologically, transcriptomically and physiologically similar to bipolar and amacrine/ganglion-like neurons. These results represent a key step forward in developing a cellular reprogramming approach for regenerative medicine in the CNS.","affiliation":"Department of Neurobiology and Biophysics, University of Washington, Seattle, WA, USA.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"HHS | NIH | National Eye Institute","grantId":"NEI R01EY021482","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Gilbert Family Foundation (GFF)","grantId":"Vision Restoration Initiative LLC","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NEI NIH HHS","acronym":"EY","grantId":"R01 EY021482","orderIn":0},{"agency":"UCSF | Weill Institute for Neurosciences, University of California, San Francisco (UCSF Weill Institute)","grantId":"Weill Neurohub Fellowship","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Tenpoint Therapeutics Ltd","grantId":"no specific number","orderIn":0},{"agency":"UCSF | Weill Institute for Neurosciences, University of California, San Francisco","grantId":"Weill Neurohub Fellowship","orderIn":0},{"agency":"HHS | NIH | National Eye Institute (NEI)","grantId":"NEI R01EY021482","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Gilbert Family Foundation","grantId":"Vision Restoration Initiative LLC","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIDDK NIH HHS","acronym":"DK","grantId":"P30 DK017047","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Neuroglia","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Neurons","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Retina"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mice, Transgenic"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mice"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Dependovirus","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Transcription Factors","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Genetic Vectors"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Neurogenesis"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Ependymoglial Cells","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Retina","Neurogenesis","Reprogramming","Aav Vectors","Müller Glia"]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Transcription Factors","registryNumber":"0"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s44321-025-00209-3"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC11982270"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC11982270?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":9,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"Y","dbCrossReferenceList":{"dbName":["EMBL"]},"hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan